The acceptance suite contains an over-specific CLI oracle that can reject a valid implementation depending only on which untiered tracked manifest is reported first.

Review comment:

- [P2] Accept any offending untiered manifest — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-31-sbom-spec/scripts/sbom-survey/tests/test_cli.py:152-154
  When the incomplete tier map covers no real manifests, the CLI is only required to name the offending path, but this assertion accepts only `Cargo.toml`. A correct implementation that processes discovered paths in `git ls-files` order can fail first on `Cargo.lock` (or another tracked manifest/lockfile) and still satisfy REQ-4 by naming that path, yet this test would fail. Check stderr against the set of currently untiered tracked manifest paths rather than hard-coding one filename.
